<!-- Official TAK logo, converted from the TAK Product Center's tak-logo.svg.

     Conversion notes, because a regeneration will hit the same two things:
      * svg2vectordrawable flattened every fill to black. The white paths were restored by
        hand from the source's document order — paths 11-13 are the T, A and K glyphs, which
        black-on-black made invisible.
      * The source uses an SVG <mask> for an outside-stroke halo (path 2). VectorDrawable has
        no mask support, so it is drawn unmasked; everything after it paints on top, leaving a
        light edge that is what makes the logo's black shield outline read against this app's
        dark toolbar. Removing it makes the badge lose its edge on dark.

     Paired with the separate red/green connection dot in the flight toolbar - the logo is
     purely the brand mark and carries no state of its own. -->
